WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.117 --> 00:00:01.701
(upbeat live band music)

00:00:01.701 --> 00:00:02.534
- Wow.

00:00:02.534 --> 00:00:04.086
(audience cheers)
Wow, goodness!

00:00:04.086 --> 00:00:04.919
- You are so...

00:00:04.919 --> 00:00:06.227
Don't they look handsome?

00:00:06.227 --> 00:00:07.060
- You guys.

00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:07.893
- [Kelly] Yes.

00:00:07.893 --> 00:00:08.726
- [Matt] You guys look incredible.

00:00:08.726 --> 00:00:09.750
- [Kelly] I know.

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:11.040
Do you have family in the military?

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:12.870
- I do, my whole family is Navy.

00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:16.140
Everybody from my uncle to my grandfather.

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:18.810
My great-grandfather was a
paratrooper in World War II.

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:19.918
- [Kelly] Wow!

00:00:19.918 --> 00:00:20.751
- Which is insane to me.

00:00:20.751 --> 00:00:21.584
'Cause if you've ever
been skydiving, you know-

00:00:21.584 --> 00:00:22.417
- No, I haven't, won't.

00:00:22.417 --> 00:00:24.630
- Well if you have any
level of depression at all,

00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:25.776
I wouldn't recommend.

00:00:25.776 --> 00:00:26.609
(Al Roker's partner laughs)
(audience laughs)

00:00:26.609 --> 00:00:28.410
- So were you always funny as a kid?

00:00:28.410 --> 00:00:29.485
- [Matt] Oh yes, I-

00:00:29.485 --> 00:00:30.387
- You (indistinct) comedy?

00:00:30.387 --> 00:00:31.440
- I was in constant detention-
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:33.165
And my mom-
- Your parents.

00:00:33.165 --> 00:00:36.000
- My mom would whoop me for
days for getting detention.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:37.830
And now that same skill
that got me detention

00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:39.535
just bought her a house.

00:00:39.535 --> 00:00:41.925
- There you go, there you go!
(audience cheers)

00:00:41.925 --> 00:00:42.758
(audience claps)

00:00:42.758 --> 00:00:44.408
- Now mine was talking too much.

00:00:44.408 --> 00:00:45.399
- [Matt] Really?

00:00:45.399 --> 00:00:46.232
- Who would've thought, yes.

00:00:46.232 --> 00:00:47.065
- [Matt] Who would've guessed?

00:00:47.065 --> 00:00:48.333
- Yes, and now I'm making
money off of it, whatever.

00:00:48.333 --> 00:00:49.440
(Al Roker laughs)

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:51.330
So, did you know what you wanted to be?

00:00:51.330 --> 00:00:52.650
Did you have an idea of
what you wanted to do

00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:53.483
when you were younger?

00:00:53.483 --> 00:00:55.860
- I had no idea; I was
gonna be in television.

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:57.570
I wasn't gonna work on TV.

00:00:57.570 --> 00:00:58.403
I wanted to work in.

00:00:58.403 --> 00:01:00.930
In fact, in my freshman year of college,

00:01:00.930 --> 00:01:03.030
when I took a television
performance class,

00:01:03.030 --> 00:01:05.160
my department chairman told me, Roker,

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:07.099
you have a perfect face for radio.

00:01:07.099 --> 00:01:07.968
- Oh my God!
(people laugh)

00:01:07.968 --> 00:01:10.350
- Oh my God, well you
can't hear that enough.

00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:12.000
Whatever!

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:13.800
But you do have a great voice, actually.

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:14.633
- Well, thanks.
- That's-

00:01:14.633 --> 00:01:15.540
- I've never been crazy
about my voice, but-

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:16.620
- Oh my gosh!
- Please do (indistinct)-

00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:17.580
- I sound like a valley girl.

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:19.590
You sound like (indistinct),
it's got the low end,

00:01:19.590 --> 00:01:20.423
like, uh!

00:01:20.423 --> 00:01:21.330
- You can lull me to sleep, for sure.

00:01:21.330 --> 00:01:22.201
In the best way.

00:01:22.201 --> 00:01:23.084
- Well, I was gonna say-

00:01:23.084 --> 00:01:23.917
- In the best way possible.

00:01:23.917 --> 00:01:24.936
- I dunno if that's a comp.

00:01:24.936 --> 00:01:26.410
- No, it's a 100%-
- It is a compliment,

00:01:26.410 --> 00:01:27.360
It is a compliment.

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:28.568
- And here's the five-day forecast.

00:01:28.568 --> 00:01:29.940
(Matt and Kelly laugh)

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:32.940
- So wait, over 17 million followers,

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:34.170
that's a little,

00:01:34.170 --> 00:01:36.360
it's intimidating and kind
of overwhelming, right?

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:37.200
- A tad bit.

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:39.180
It does feel like it came out of nowhere.

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:40.590
But then I have to remind myself

00:01:40.590 --> 00:01:41.970
as much as it feels overnight,

00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:43.500
because it did happen very fast.

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:44.462
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:44.462 --> 00:01:45.295
- Via social media.

00:01:45.295 --> 00:01:47.460
I'd been doing comedy
for 12 years before that.

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:48.293
- Yeah.

00:01:48.293 --> 00:01:49.126
- So anytime I feel overwhelmed

00:01:49.126 --> 00:01:51.600
about people coming up on
the streets or at restaurants

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:52.470
or something like that,

00:01:52.470 --> 00:01:54.180
and they ask me, "Oh, I'm
so sorry to bother you."

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:55.350
I'm like, no, you're not a bother at all.

00:01:55.350 --> 00:01:57.408
For 11 years I begged somebody to take-

00:01:57.408 --> 00:01:58.459
(Al Roker laughs)

00:01:58.459 --> 00:01:59.760
You kidding me?
- Notice me.

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:01.470
- Yeah, you know what's worse
than everybody knowing you.

00:02:01.470 --> 00:02:02.303
Nobody knowing you.

00:02:02.303 --> 00:02:03.270
- Yeah.
(Al Roker's partner laughs)

00:02:03.270 --> 00:02:05.790
- It's amazing, this is the
first special for Netflix.

00:02:05.790 --> 00:02:07.290
And I couldn't be more excited;

00:02:07.290 --> 00:02:08.790
because I think, again,
it's just gonna broaden me

00:02:08.790 --> 00:02:09.720
to a different audience,

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:11.850
that either sees me as
just a TikTok comedian

00:02:11.850 --> 00:02:13.650
or someone who just does crowd work.

00:02:13.650 --> 00:02:15.000
I think they're gonna
be pleasantly surprised

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:15.930
at what else I can do.

00:02:15.930 --> 00:02:16.763
- Oh, I love that.

00:02:16.763 --> 00:02:19.410
And I love that, when
people underestimate you,

00:02:19.410 --> 00:02:20.430
'cause then it's like fun

00:02:20.430 --> 00:02:21.342
and it fuels you.

00:02:21.342 --> 00:02:22.175
- [Matt] Oh, of course.

00:02:22.175 --> 00:02:23.008
- And you wanna win them over.

00:02:23.008 --> 00:02:23.880
- Oh yeah, that's the
best revenge, success.

00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:26.670
- The underdog is always a
better position in my opinion.

00:02:26.670 --> 00:02:27.503
- [Matt] Oh, of course.

00:02:27.503 --> 00:02:28.336
- Speaking of his fans, though,

00:02:28.336 --> 00:02:29.940
this happened recently
at one of Matt's shows.

00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:31.477
Watch this.

00:02:31.477 --> 00:02:33.926
- [Patron] And she has wanted you

00:02:33.926 --> 00:02:35.597
to figure out how to-

00:02:35.597 --> 00:02:37.208
- [Matt] Oh, (bleep).

00:02:37.208 --> 00:02:38.041
- [Patron] Original (indistinct).

00:02:38.041 --> 00:02:39.570
- Yo, can we get a paramedic real quick?

00:02:39.570 --> 00:02:40.898
Paramedic, please?

00:02:40.898 --> 00:02:41.779
You okay?

00:02:41.779 --> 00:02:42.612
- [Attendee] Oh, she's gonna cry in here.

00:02:42.612 --> 00:02:43.801
- [Matt] You all right?

00:02:43.801 --> 00:02:44.634
(attendee laughs)

00:02:44.634 --> 00:02:46.579
You feeling okay, you promise?

00:02:46.579 --> 00:02:47.717
- [Attendee] Can she
get a picture with you?

00:02:47.717 --> 00:02:49.519
- Yeah (giggles), of course.

00:02:49.519 --> 00:02:51.317
Just don't use it for
the obituary, my God.

00:02:51.317 --> 00:02:52.469
(people laugh)

00:02:52.469 --> 00:02:54.177
(people clap)

00:02:54.177 --> 00:02:55.768
- That's the best line.
(audience cheers)

00:02:55.768 --> 00:02:56.629
What happened?

00:02:56.629 --> 00:02:58.589
(audience claps)

00:02:58.589 --> 00:03:01.380
- Well she's okay.

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:02.213
She's fine.

00:03:02.213 --> 00:03:03.360
- Which is why the joke is funny.

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:04.680
- Yeah, oh, of course, of course.

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:05.820
No, we wouldn't have continued the show

00:03:05.820 --> 00:03:07.470
if someone (bleep) happens.

00:03:07.470 --> 00:03:09.348
Like, somebody get her outta
here, I gotta plug merch.

00:03:09.348 --> 00:03:10.181
(Kelly laughs)

00:03:10.181 --> 00:03:11.370
No, no, I, no,

00:03:11.370 --> 00:03:12.374
this looks-

00:03:12.374 --> 00:03:13.567
(audience laughs)

00:03:13.567 --> 00:03:15.317
(Al Roker claps loudly)

00:03:15.317 --> 00:03:16.557
Cut!

00:03:16.557 --> 00:03:18.109
Cut, rewind it.
- That's amazing!

00:03:18.109 --> 00:03:18.942
That's amazing.

00:03:18.942 --> 00:03:20.760
- This was probably 25 minutes

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:22.680
into one of our headlining shows.

00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:25.050
And I hear this commotion and I look down

00:03:25.050 --> 00:03:27.360
and I could see she's convulsing.

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:29.580
So I immediately, once I
recognized what was happening,

00:03:29.580 --> 00:03:31.500
I called for anybody being
a paramedic in the room.

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:33.270
And luckily the people in the venue

00:03:33.270 --> 00:03:34.860
and people who do work
in the medical field,

00:03:34.860 --> 00:03:35.850
that were in the audience,

00:03:35.850 --> 00:03:37.410
rushed to her side immediately.

00:03:37.410 --> 00:03:39.600
I have to leave the
stage when that happens,

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:41.850
so that I can be informed
as to what's going on.

00:03:41.850 --> 00:03:43.410
While she's getting tended to properly-

00:03:43.410 --> 00:03:44.281
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:44.281 --> 00:03:45.114
- And not in anybody's way.

00:03:45.114 --> 00:03:47.370
And it was like seven
or eight minutes later,

00:03:47.370 --> 00:03:49.710
I would say, my security came back

00:03:49.710 --> 00:03:52.797
and was like, "Hey,
she, she wants to stay."

00:03:52.797 --> 00:03:53.630
(people chuckle)

00:03:53.630 --> 00:03:55.110
I was like, I'll give her a refund.

00:03:55.110 --> 00:03:57.150
Like she doesn't have to stay.

00:03:57.150 --> 00:03:58.410
But she, I went out there, I was like,

00:03:58.410 --> 00:03:59.940
lemme just go talk to her,
make sure she's all right.

00:03:59.940 --> 00:04:01.560
And I walked out and the
first thing I said was like,

00:04:01.560 --> 00:04:02.393
are you okay?

00:04:02.393 --> 00:04:05.220
She was like, "Yeah,
can I have a picture?"

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:07.739
I was like, yeah, no flash.
(Kelly laughs)

00:04:07.739 --> 00:04:09.660
(audience laughs)

00:04:09.660 --> 00:04:10.680
She had epilepsy.

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:13.200
What a wild thing to ask first, man.

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:16.440
But you go, you gotta, you
gotta respect the passion.

00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:17.273
She wanted to stay.

00:04:17.273 --> 00:04:19.110
She had carpe diem.

00:04:19.110 --> 00:04:21.030
- Comedy makes people happy.

00:04:21.030 --> 00:04:21.863
You make people happy-
- [Matt] Of course.

00:04:21.863 --> 00:04:22.696
- You make people laugh.

00:04:22.696 --> 00:04:24.750
I forgot this and I went to a
show here recently in New York

00:04:24.750 --> 00:04:27.390
and it made me feel so good
to get out and just laugh.

00:04:27.390 --> 00:04:28.223
- [Al] With other people.

00:04:28.223 --> 00:04:29.056
- Yes.
- Oh, absolutely.

00:04:29.056 --> 00:04:29.889
You have no idea.

00:04:29.889 --> 00:04:30.722
It brings people together

00:04:30.722 --> 00:04:31.555
to such an extreme level.

00:04:31.555 --> 00:04:32.388
You'd think it's just-

00:04:32.388 --> 00:04:33.221
- [Kelly] Yes.

00:04:33.221 --> 00:04:34.054
- Random jokes that you're just telling

00:04:34.054 --> 00:04:34.887
to make people happy.

00:04:34.887 --> 00:04:35.720
- [Kelly] No we're all connecting-

00:04:35.720 --> 00:04:36.553
- You have no idea what
people are going through.

00:04:36.553 --> 00:04:37.386
- [Kelly] In a different way.

00:04:37.386 --> 00:04:38.219
- Yes, absolutely.

00:04:38.219 --> 00:04:39.450
She was such a good
sport about everything.

00:04:39.450 --> 00:04:41.520
- It's actually happened
at a show for like,

00:04:41.520 --> 00:04:43.560
it shows for me like you're
in live situations too.

00:04:43.560 --> 00:04:44.760
Where things have happened like that

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:45.960
and you get, you freaked out.

00:04:45.960 --> 00:04:47.490
'Cause you're like, well
wait 'cause loud music.

00:04:47.490 --> 00:04:48.570
I'm like, make it go away.

00:04:48.570 --> 00:04:49.403
- It's just stop.

00:04:49.403 --> 00:04:50.236
Please stop.
- Yeah.

00:04:50.236 --> 00:04:51.237
- Oh these kind of things
happen all the time.

00:04:51.237 --> 00:04:54.688
We had an overdose in Indianapolis-

00:04:54.688 --> 00:04:55.521
- Ooh!

00:04:55.521 --> 00:04:56.354
- Like two weeks ago.

00:04:56.354 --> 00:04:58.890
And the audience was furious
that he did not offer

00:04:58.890 --> 00:05:00.045
to share with the rest of the crowd.

00:05:00.045 --> 00:05:01.676
(people shout)

00:05:01.676 --> 00:05:02.648
They were so mad.

00:05:02.648 --> 00:05:03.481
- Whoa!

00:05:03.481 --> 00:05:06.060
- I had no idea
Indianapolis was so ratchet.

00:05:06.060 --> 00:05:07.353
Like they were so upset.

00:05:08.899 --> 00:05:09.732
- [Kelly] But I (indistinct)!

00:05:09.732 --> 00:05:11.370
- Like, usually people
rally behind something.

00:05:11.370 --> 00:05:12.960
They're like, "Yeah,
make sure he is okay."

00:05:12.960 --> 00:05:14.789
And they were like, "Selfish."

00:05:14.789 --> 00:05:15.817
- Selfish!

00:05:15.817 --> 00:05:18.229
Oh my God, you're so funny (laughs)!

00:05:18.229 --> 00:05:19.859
- [Matt] I know, it was so ridiculous.

00:05:19.859 --> 00:05:20.939
- Matt Rife everybody.

00:05:20.939 --> 00:05:21.877
(crowd shouts)

00:05:21.877 --> 00:05:25.877
"Natural Selection", on
Netflix, starting November 15th.

00:05:25.877 --> 00:05:29.700
You gotta check it out!
(audience claps)

